    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "As an insider on the subject of regulatory policy in the medical world, and through extensive research into the situation, the author exposes the seriously troubling and, so far, unaddressed difficulty of a complex FDA regulatory framework that was not formed to deal with and is not capable of, addressing the urgency or complexity of Artificial Intelligence (AI)-enabled medical devices in off-label use. \r\n\r\nThis thesis paints a picture of the increasingly powerful and mysterious use of AI in Clinical Decision Support Systems (CDSS) and Software as a Medical Device (SaMD), illustrating through case studies the growing difficulty of doctors and patients alike in making informed decisions about medical treatment, whose determinations are an AI mystery and cannot be penetrated even by very sophisticated thought. \r\n\r\nThis thesis explains 1) the unregulated off-label use of drugs and medical devices, 2) the current situation in which dependence on AI equals dependence on inexplicable non-human decisions that patients or doctors cannot rationally consider, and 3) the inadequacy of current FDA regulations to protect patients and the medical community from the dangers of such a situation. \r\n\r\nThis thesis presents a compelling argument about the urgent need for better regulation of AI and Machine Learning (ML) software functions in healthcare, especially in off-label use. Through extensive research and case studies, it highlights the growing challenges faced by doctors and patients in making informed decisions, emphasizing the ethical, social, and practical implications of this issue and calls for the responsible development and regulation of AI in a rapidly emerging and disquieting problematic space.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
